+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more groups of a whole number followed by a unit: `d` for days, `h` for
+hours, `m` for minutes, and `s` for seconds. Each unit may be given at most once, in that order, without spaces, such
+as `2d`, `1h30m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Units are case-insensitive. Negative numbers and decimals are not accepted.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
